/* Model-owned refinements/collector-work declarations; imported by shared-heap-smp.sysml. */
package GambitSharedHeapSmpCollectorWorkRefinement {
 private import GambitSharedHeapSmp::*;

 part queueObservationToIdle:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="queueObservationToIdle";
  attribute :>> precondition="Exact VM/collection/phase, target queue and live control storage; initialized publication and unique claim; caller counted active; no unresolved prior take may be overwritten";
  attribute :>> argument="Acquired transfers only the selected node from publisher queue custody to active claimant private debt. ConfirmedEmpty requires acquired queue exclusion and empty head/tail at its linearization; it is scoped to queue/phase/revision. Unobserved is a known failed gate acquisition: this operation performs no custody transfer, while other operations may still change the queue. Local idle joins a fresh own-queue empty observation with private/frontier/still/initialization/Tail drain. Publish revokes prior empty evidence; busy is never upgraded to empty. Lost delivery after a committed claim is unsettled operation state, not an Unobserved result; retain counted claimant, node/arena/root/control lifetime until identity settlement.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Existing QNT distinguishes the three outcomes and prevents stale empty or unsettled claim from authorizing idle; existing Lean QueuePost relates each linearized operation to its data transfer without a second state machine";
  attribute :>> missing="Current C still collapses busy and acquired-empty to zero. Implement or establish an authoritative owner-drain interface, exact return/claim mapping and publication invalidation before idle. Ghost revisions and phase witnesses are model evidence, not new runtime fields or a proposed identity table. Complete unknown-before-commit and physical owner-stop adapters remain OPEN.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One whole queue-result/local-drain/idle/phase/exit packet: busy with queued work retains publisher; acquired result retains private debt; confirmed empty cannot settle Tail; publish/phase reuse invalidates old evidence; committed result loss blocks finish/retry/idle until exact settlement; native last users remain covered by existing retirement gates";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="QNT owns freshness, transition ordering and unsettled custody; Lean owns QueuePost data preservation/count conservation. A no-effect law compares this operation's linearized projection, not arbitrary concurrent snapshots. Source factors and all five joint obligations remain distinct and OPEN.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Interpreting failed own-gate CAS as confirmed empty permits a queued custodian to idle. Reusing an empty observation after publication/phase change is stale. Treating a lost committed-claim response as Unobserved permits duplicate execution or early reclaim; a gate holder does not automatically own every node in that queue.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=chunkClaim;
  ref part :>> exitSite=lastWorkerIdle;
 }
 part queueCallerAdapter:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="queueCallerAdapter";
  attribute :>> precondition="One private C interface replacement covers both direct take callers, publisher, initialization, restoration and round-storage retirement; exact worker/target identity and configured synchronization lifetime are admitted";
  attribute :>> argument="Keep take_heap_chunk as the existing internal operation and change its contract to a typed status plus nonaliasing caller-owned chunk output. Clear output on non-acquired results; use one gate-protected claim/head-removal core and release the gate before scan. Owner drain handles Unobserved by retaining cursor, count and work custody until authoritative reprobe; thieves may skip a busy or empty victim without treating either as local drain. Install existing active_scan_chunk/scan_origin claim custody before queue removal is externally complete; scan_complete validates and completes that claim. scan_movable returns only after authoritative own-empty and complete movable frontier; mark_reachable's outer still/movable loop supplies the combined local fixed point, including synchronous initialization/Tail closure. Nonterminal wake refreshes that cut before another idle decrement. Phase barriers then authorize restoration observations; fresh setup and cleanup_rc cannot reset/free VM-owned workers while any publisher, waiter, claimant, returning native user or unsettled take can still access them.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="A complete private queue/scan/termination/lifecycle adapter is specified without changing Scheme scheduling policy, public Scheme names, heap limits, wait budgets or introducing a parallel namespace; it is not implemented by this research";
  attribute :>> missing="Current C pointer-or-zero interface, both callsites, claim-registration return gap, cursor-only local return, wake-to-steal route and raw post-phase head/tail check must all refine the chosen contract. Current preflight checks copy/arena/Tail debt but is not a proof that queue gates, active claims and native last users have closed. No unknown internal fragment can be repaired merely by forcing a gate open or clearing the worker array.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One responsibility delivery validates acquired/busy/empty at both real callsites, private claim visible across return loss, no scan/copy/callback while queue gate held, owner fixed-point drain and wake refresh, W<R source restoration, strong/weak phase identity, fresh storage setup and delayed last-user free. Reuse existing component/Scheme consumers only after current-source interface qualification; deterministic gate-contention and actual private-operation test access remain native acceptance requirements.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing QNT localDrainReady and phaseClosed own temporal admission; QueuePost owns data transfer. Source must supply actual C status/out-pointer decoding, linked-layout coverage, selected acquire/release and last-user correspondence. No QNT/Lean duplicate or model-only C qualification is introduced.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Only changing the return type leaves an owner that exits on busy unsafe. Recording the claim only inside scan_complete leaves the removed-before-call interval unrepresented. Reading head/tail without whole-phase last-user closure, or memset/free during an unknown gate/claim outcome, invalidates the empty or storage-lifetime premise.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=localQueueDrain;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerStorageRetire;
 }
 part claimInterruptionSettlement:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="claimInterruptionSettlement";
  attribute :>> precondition="Caller knows a fixed worker-slot operation key before the fallible call; VM/control entry pins storage before pointer access. Immutable key/item/queue fields are initialized before release-publishing an intent. At most one unsettled take per worker; original and helper writers require exclusive generation authority.";
  attribute :>> argument="Current C changes chunk state, then head, chunks_claimed, gate and return; later scan_complete records active private work. The adapter needs a bounded take slot in the VM-owned worker, keyed by VM incarnation/collection/phase/worker/generation. Published intent is not claim authority. Successful chunk1->2 transfers logical custody even while linkage remains; head removal does not finish it. Progress may lag each real store: query reports partial, never reissues take. Commit decision is separate from last gate-use publication and result delivery. Exact-key pinned query observes immutable data without queue mutation; settlement after known commit/release delivers the same claim once. Source-closed helpers may finish the existing fragment only after original/helper permits close; unknown owner retains counted work, gate, arena and enclosing round.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Existing QNT exposes log-lag windows and read-only repeated queries; existing Lean immutable-key lookup laws cannot return a different recorded item. This specifies a complete bounded settlement protocol, not an existing native query API or a physical-stop theorem.";
  attribute :>> missing="Current active_scan_chunk/origin lack operation key, immutable decision, gate-use and query-grace information. Add or establish that fixed-slot representation; do not conflate pointer presence, diagnostic chunks_claimed, physical gate zero, or a lagging progress word with committed/closed status. Real immutable publication, CAS/store readback, nonwrapping identity, entry closure, helper exclusion and slot retirement remain source/native duties.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One packet covers interruption before intent publication, after chunk claim before progress log, after unlink before log, after commit before release, after release before closure receipt, lost result, duplicate query/delivery, stale key and slot pin. Known unclaimed abort keeps publisher; postclaim uncertainty keeps VM claim custody. Native helpers require independently established writer closure and no late stores; keep all five joint acceptance obligations OPEN until actual qualification.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="QNT uses atomic source-effect and separate log-effect microsteps but not individual machine instructions, torn fields or C weak memory. Completed atomic acquire remains the existing abstraction; interrupted paths refine its pending boundary. Lean proves immutable receipt lookup/data identity only. Existing retirement models own native last-user premises; owner knowledge loss is a no-authority observation, not a certified stop.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A stage1 record can coexist with an already claimed linked node, so rollback/reclaim from stage1 alone is invalid. Gate zero does not prove the original postlude stopped. Retrying chunks_claimed++ after a lost progress write can double accounting. A vacant/stale slot observation does not prove no late admission; reuse before query grace can turn an old key into another claim.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=chunkClaim;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerStorageRetire;
 }
 part takeSlotPublicationRetirement:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="takeSlotPublicationRetirement";
  attribute :>> precondition="Existing VM/control lifetime pins the enclosing round before slot address use; one allocated worker slot and nonwrapping operation identity; every owner/helper/observer uses the same atomic access and admission protocol";
  attribute :>> argument="Layout separates immutable key/intent from atomic query gate, exclusive writer gate, writer generation, decision and gate-use closure. Query gate combines closed bit and reader count in one CAS word: pin storage before key check, seal without erasing old pins, mutate/reuse only after closed-and-zero. Writer gate closes new entries but preserves the current borrower; validate operation key and writer generation after pin, then write. Rotate helper generation only while writer gate closed and empty; operation key stays unchanged. Initialize header before release-opening query admission, initialize intent before release-publishing its readiness, and read plain payload only after acquiring the corresponding readiness while pinned. Terminal stage/zero pins alone cannot retire live claim work, an unclosed writer or unknown gate use.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Existing QNT now exposes pin-before-key, seal/drain, writer-generation handoff, helper interruption and explicit slot retirement; Lean checks closed-bit/count encoding only. This is a concrete access-class/layout contract with no runtime implementation or additional global identity table.";
  attribute :>> missing="Map logical atomic words consistently to the existing ordered-word/full-RMW service and selected C23 compiler/backend; no volatile-only synchronization or plain/atomic mixture. Prove actual prefix publication, all writer enrollment, no post-release slot access, count/generation overflow rejection, VM address admission and arbitrary query-reader grace. Unknown borrowed writer cannot be declared drained from timeout or join alone.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One packet races pin versus seal, delayed key validation versus reuse, seal versus original/helper release, stale helper entry after generation rotation, unknown helper retention, completed claim versus zero-query counters, phase seal and fresh key publication. Preserve every existing queue/claim test and source/native gate; finite one-reader model support is not a native drain certificate.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="QNT owns transitions/exclusion; Lean gateEncodingInjective and sealedGateZeroHasNoBorrowers own Nat encoding data, not atomic interleavings. Current C lifecycle entries show a related closed-bit/+2 pattern, not a take-slot implementation or its correctness proof. Actual layout offsets/bytes and compiler atomics remain qualified-source obligations.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Check key before pin permits reuse between check and read. Separate close/count sampling can miss an arriving reader. Clearing a closed gate erases an old borrower. Checking helper generation before pin permits stale reentry after reopen. A seqlock retry cannot legalize concurrent plain payload reads/writes in C23.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=takeAtomicService;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerStorageRetire;
 }
 part takeSlotAtomicServiceMap:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="takeSlotAtomicServiceMap";
  attribute :>> precondition="Naturally aligned existing word storage and one selected native or legacy provider; immutable header/intent prefixes, exact operation key and live enclosing storage; no plain concurrent control access";
  attribute :>> argument="Map acquired decision/generation reads to WORD_LOAD_ACQUIRE, immutable-prefix/open publication to WORD_STORE_RELEASE and last borrower release to WORD_FETCH_ADD_RELEASE(-2). Gate pin/seal and once-only decision transitions use the existing observed-value COMPARE_AND_SWAP_WORD contract with failure reload, not an assumed expected-argument update. Native WORD_CAS_ACQUIRE is acquire-only and changes expected on failure; its legacy expression does not provide identical expected-variable behavior. Emulated qualification uses same-address mutex edges; the checkout C23 seq_cst fence is not quiescence or a complete publication/data-race proof. The captured historical cache has an empty fence implementation, inactive in its selected sync branch. Guard old<=checkedWordLimit-2 before add2 and generation<limit before successor; exhaustion retains/refuses rather than wrapping. Late owner/helper pins storage before checking key and writer generation; an unvalidated pin grants no payload write and still blocks drain. Helper generation resets only under complete slot retirement and a fresh operation key, never while an old operation or borrow survives.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Existing QNT checks post-pin validation and responsibility retention after refused admission at generation/capacity boundaries; Lean alone proves bounded addition and strict-successor arithmetic. The provider mapping is explicit but source/ABI/compiler qualification remains OPEN.";
  attribute :>> missing="Prove concrete WORD width/alignment/accessor ABI, each same-object release/acquire chain, native and forced-legacy compiler paths, alias discipline, failure-return handling, count underflow/double-release exclusion and a pre-destructive-GC generation headroom/refusal strategy. A finite test ceiling is not a runtime knob. No bounded recovery under arbitrary helper failure is claimed.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One packet covers CAS-failure expected behavior, admission refusal with old custody retained, operation/helper generation exhaustion, stale owner key after reuse, stale helper token after reopen, unvalidated pin retention, prefix acquisition and actual provider code generation. Unsupported or unknown provider behavior remains unresolved; no sequential-backend SMP attestation.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Quint ceiling3 is a small qualification horizon for exhaustion histories, not an implementation constant. Lean Nat boundedness is conditional on the checked field limit. Neither proves finite C integer semantics or selected compiler memory behavior; both C support factors and five joint questions stay OPEN.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Computing old+2 before checking the cap can overflow; wrapping helper generation revives an old token. Reopening the writer gate without post-pin key/generation validation permits late data access. Relying on native expected mutation in a legacy CAS loop can spin on stale expected. Counter zero or a free physical gate does not authorize raw stale pointers.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=orderedCasFailureContract;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerStorageRetire;
 }
 part takeSlotCSettlement:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="takeSlotCSettlement";
  attribute :>> precondition="Live VM/round address admission precedes slot access; selected ordered-word and full-CAS operations interoperate on the same naturally aligned field; original/helper writers and queries hold separately owned borrows; source-bound compiler/target/word/thread/macro expansion identifies both actual provider selections; provider setup has completed and its synchronization resources outlive every enrolled accessor";
  attribute :>> argument="Current take_heap_chunk holds owner chunk_gate while changing chunk state1->2, replacing head and incrementing chunks_claimed, then unlocks and returns; scan_complete_heap_chunk registers active_scan_chunk only later. A replacement must register immutable operation key/intent before the first queue effect and retain source-closed reconciliation authority across each effect/log window. Claimed-linked, detached, committed, gate-closed and delivered are distinct outcomes. Exact-key query is read-only and returns pending or a recorded outcome, never a second take. A stage value alone cannot tell whether its following physical effect happened. Last writer release follows its final data/log touch; query seal preserves old pins. Writer generation rotates only after old writer admission is closed and drained; slot retirement additionally waits query grace, terminal work transfer and enclosing last users. Full-CAS selection follows word width and GCC sync feature macros, otherwise Win32/POSIX-emulated/sequential; ordered-word selection independently follows ATOMIC feature macros and legacy override. setup_thread_module initializes emulated hash mutexes; cleanup_thread_module destroys them when its module refcount reaches zero. rc_can_close checks round/RC/census state but contains no take-slot reader/writer predicate, and root_round_end returns to IDLE after root restoration without a take receipt drain. Neither existing check can stand in for the proposed slot grace. cleanup_runtime and cleanup_os_and_mem must retain actual provider resources until all unresolved slot users are excluded.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="The concrete queue mutation/return/registration interval and existing provider/lifecycle primitives are now one source-refinement chain. Retained review classifies 82 occurrences in 9 files; actual Make-derived cache preprocessing captures both TUs selecting native ordered-word plus sync CAS, with an original12 checkout input mismatches and no object/link/runtime acceptance; after another owner updates os_thread.c, two recaptured TUs still select native+sync with 11 mismatches remaining. Exact attribution separates 5 line-coordinate-only inputs from 7 configured/semantic inputs. Generated checkout gambit.h is a different single-VM/single-threaded artifact; canonical header inputs additionally remove obsolete native_scope storage, so neither stale generated output nor cached layout can be copied as current authority. mem.c is the actual collector TU including the ordered .inc fragments; os_thread.c is a separate provider TU. Their effective provider records must agree on shared word layout, operation interoperability and linked provider availability. Current C has no fixed-slot operation receipt or exact-key settlement query; this case specifies replacement requirements without claiming runtime implementation.";
  attribute :>> missing="Runtime patch boundary is collector.h, the mem.c include consumers, existing atomic service/provider and root/VM teardown integration, plus existing fixtures; exclude scheduler policy, generational policy and unrelated FFI redesign. Implement one VM-owned per-worker record and its lifecycle in the runtime-owning thread; bind physical effects to immutable before/after identity and idempotent settlement under actual writer exclusion; route both take callers through typed outcomes and install private scan custody before delivery ACK. Qualify cross-family atomic interoperability: native ordered loads/stores mixed with mutex-emulated ordinary-access RMW are not admitted merely by two macro names. Check retained VM/round storage, source-only plain access under queue gate, fatal-hook escape and exact outer last users. Current maintained references to chunks_claimed/completed are declarations, increments and resets, with no decision consumer found; preserve that diagnostic-only status. A possibly repeated diagnostic increment must be marked unresolved or reconciled, never made ownership/termination authority or blindly replayed. External/unqualified readers remain outside this finding. Bind selection and setup/teardown to the same source period and exact translation unit, not an unrelated configure cache. Owner-controlled source-delta synchronization must refresh canonical generator inputs/configuration and regenerate the header in the same build product, then recapture both TUs; coordinate-only changes still invalidate exact expanded bytes and diagnostic coordinates. Emulated arithmetic/fence changes require separate admission only for that backend; no emulated performance cause is established for the observed native+sync path. Extend round end/refusal, queue reset, RC prepare/free and global provider teardown with the actual slot-last-user predicate; preserve pre-copy refusal as a no-effect path, not a rollback of partial claims. Unknown query/writer or held shared gate retains the affected VM and provider dependencies; a known join alone does not settle a possibly completed effect.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One whole patch acceptance packet binds mem.c and os_thread.c actual build requests, expanded provider operations and link/runtime artifact identity; it covers both callers, original/helper late pin validation, each physical-effect/log interruption, gate release before return, delivery before ACK, slot reuse, unknown stop and native last use. Exact-key repeated queries must not change queue/copy ownership; known stale key rejects only after storage admission; unknown access keeps the affected slot/round alive. Preserve original budgets and all five joint acceptance obligations; no whole-VM independence claim while shared gate ownership remains unknown. Include fresh setup, setup rollback, repeated round reuse, local cleanup refusal and final global cleanup with the selected provider; all payload/gate postludes finish before their enclosing storage or emulation mutex is destroyed. A nonterminal pending claim remains represented in phase termination and cannot disappear at idle decrement.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Consume existing QNT custody/interleaving histories and Lean representation/arithmetic laws only. This case owns concrete C correspondence, including field widths, selected providers and actual interruption guards; it does not add temporal or arithmetic proofs. Native execution and matched cost remain independent evidence.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A stage1 record may coexist with a claimed linked node; retrying take loses or double-claims work. Head already advanced plus missing log cannot justify a second counter increment. A free chunk gate does not prove old postlude completion. Matching numeric generation does not pin a freed VM. A mutex-protected plain RMW and unrelated compiler atomic access do not establish a common admission protocol by declaration alone. Freeing the VM round while a query is pinned causes stale storage access; retaining the round but destroying its emulated hash mutex still invalidates the service. ROOT_ROUND_IDLE and a successful join are not a fixed-slot drain certificate.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=chunkClaim;
  ref part :>> exitSite=latePrivateClaimRegistration;
 }
 part wholeWorkPublication:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="wholeWorkPublication";
  attribute :>> precondition="Fixed accepted VM/collection/phase membership; every private copier, Tail, local frontier, dequeued scanner and external producer is covered by an active owner or accepted transfer; destination scan metadata initialized for this collection";
  attribute :>> argument="publish_object_scan changes initialized movable identity UNPUBLISHED->READY; scan claims READY->OWNED and repeats return without field mutation. end_heap_chunk closes the boundary, changes chunk0->1 and publishes link/tail under chunk_gate plus ordering barriers; take_heap_chunk changes1->2 before removing queue reachability. Local/incomplete frontier and active_scan_chunk remain private obligations. mark_reachable_from_marked scans local/still work, steals then decrements the phase counter under scan_termination_mutex; only an active counted owner may publish new work. All R root sources and recovery spans remain distinct from W scanning workers.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="A complete producer-lifetime adapter could justify phase termination and avoid repeated movable field mutation; existing source mechanisms are candidates, not a verified all-producer closure";
  attribute :>> missing="The abstract idle mismatch is corrected in the existing QNT: localDrained includes private, queued and claimed work owned by this worker; producerCoverage retains every other item's counted custodian. Successful acquire transfers to an active claimant; failed CAS is an observation-free stutter; nonterminal wake needs no queue predicate. This yields a conditional counted-work simulation, not a total C proof. Still establish actual scan_ptr/cursor and FIFO-layout drain, all private/Tail/weak/helper producers, initialized release/acquire visibility, successful wait behavior, fixed phase membership and no old-phase last user. The phase token is a logical witness, not an implemented C check. Unknown claim/stop retains data and synchronization resources; do not decrement its authority on timeout. Strong zero/DRAINING still precedes weak, restore and cleanup.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Conjoin both C factors on one exact source/backend/epoch; existing gc_work_closure local-idle/spurious-wake/late-phase histories, WorkAccounting private-plus-published coverage algebra and existing last-consumer/quarantine histories supply distinct premises. Require real last-publish/busy-gate/idle/wake, weak will discovery, restore/cleanup and known/unknown-stop controls with exact custodians. Phase barriers and native last users need source qualification. Preserve healthy independent-VM collection and all five joint native/cost gates; no source pass from model support";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="GW-S retains source ownership. Existing gc_work_closure checks localDrained, queued/private producerCoverage, nonterminal spurious wake and phase witness in a finite atomic model. WorkAccounting derives empty queues from zero and published/private lifetime coverage, rather than assuming a global queue snapshot. Existing last-user/quarantine slices preserve their separate temporal owners; their join to current C identity/lifetime is a source premise. No arbitrary R/W, C memory order, native stop or fairness theorem is implied.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="An uncounted private producer permits false zero and late publication; a busy gate is not empty. A signal before wait need not wake that waiter, but a current-C lost-work claim also requires disproving the active publisher's own-drain route: no reachable native bug is inferred here. Strong zero cannot authorize reuse while weak production or restore remains. data_closed may be visible before the launching thread unlocks the VM gate; reclaiming the descriptor or mutex at that point can outlive its proof. Duplicate scan skip does not settle Tail or initialization.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=rootCollective;
  ref part :>> exitSite=rootEnd;
 }
}
